  "prompt_text": "Use case: precise-object-edit.\nAsset type: transparent whole-animal sprite sheet in the WorldSim stone-age ink-and-tone family.\nInputs: Image1 is the edit target, the existing ten dun horse sprites in two rows and five columns. Image2 and Image3 are locked style references only.\nPrimary request: change ONLY the tiny hide hatch clusters on each of the ten horses. The existing sheet has two main groups and scattered dots. REPLACE the body hatch with EXACTLY THREE localized groups on every horse: one on shoulder, one on central flank, one on haunch. Each of those three groups contains EXACTLY THREE short simple unbroken parallel ink strokes slanting from upper-left to lower-right. Nine body strokes total per horse, arranged as three separated groups. Each stroke continuous: no dot/dash pairs, no broken strokes, no dots. Remove scattered decorative chest/neck ink ticks outside those groups; keep natural anatomical and facial lines intact. Keep the marks delicate, secondary in weight to the silhouette, much smaller than the leg contours.\nSTRICT INVARIANTS: preserve the ten whole horses, all sizes, identities and poses, full outlines, coat wash, palette, mane and tail silhouettes, faces, legs, hooves, positions and spacing. Two rows, five columns unchanged. Top S row: stand, walk, run, graze, dead. Bottom E row same order. Do not alter anatomy, poses, camera, scale or drawing style. Natural primitive dun horses with short dark upright manes and dark tails; no tack or horseshoes. Upper-left lighting. Dark brown main contour approximately twice interior details. Preserve restrained earth wash.\nOutput true transparent RGBA, without background color, backdrop, ground, ground shadows, letters, guides or panels. Keep broad transparent gutters and full figures. The sole artwork change is correcting the hide hatch rule to exactly three groups of three continuous strokes on each horse.\n",
